            "text": "<BEGIN_SHACL>\n@prefix sh: <http://www.w3.org/ns/shacl#> .\n@prefix xsd: <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .\n@prefix qudt: <http://qudt.org/schema/qudt/> .\n@prefix unit: <http://qudt.org/vocab/unit/> .\n@prefix nltl: <https://w3id.org/nltl/vocab#> .\n\nnltl:TRF035ShipShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:targetClass nltl:ship ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:ruleLength ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:node nltl:TRF035LengthQuantityShape ;\n        sh:message \"The ship's L value shall be represented as its rule length used by the classification society (TRF-035, clause 4.1.1).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:classificationSociety ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:string ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:message \"If provided, the classification society shall be represented as a string (TRF-035, clause 4.1.1).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path nltl:classificationSocietyRuleLength ;\n        sh:node nltl:TRF035LengthQuantityShape ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:message \"If provided, the classification-society rule length shall be represented as a metre-based quantity (TRF-035, clause 4.1.1).\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:description \"Representation of TRF-035, TRAFICOM page 13, clause 4.1.1. The source identifies L with the ship's rule length used by the classification society. The supplied mappings contain both ruleLength and classificationSocietyRuleLength; no equality constraint between them is asserted.\" .\n\nnltl:TRF035LengthQuantityShape\n    a sh:NodeShape ;\n    sh:class qudt:QuantityValue ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:numericValue ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:datatype xsd:decimal ;\n        sh:message \"A rule length quantity shall have exactly one decimal numeric value.\" ;\n    ] ;\n    sh:property [\n        sh:path qudt:unit ;\n        sh:minCount 1 ;\n        sh:maxCount 1 ;\n        sh:hasValue unit:M ;\n        sh:message \"A rule length quantity shall use the canonical QUDT metre unit.\" ;\n    ] .\n<END_SHACL>"
